# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hosted free analyses. HOSTED_PROVIDER_API_KEY and FREE_RUN_SECRET must both
# be set for a visitor without their own API key to run anything —
# HOSTED_PROVIDER falls back to the app default when unset. Leave them unset
# and the app still works — it just runs in bring-your-own-key mode and
# reports HOSTED_UNAVAILABLE honestly rather than pretending a visitor spent
# an allowance they never had.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The provider key that serves free hosted analyses.
#
# SET A SPEND LIMIT ON THIS KEY IN THE PROVIDER CONSOLE. That limit — not any
# code in this repository — is the real ceiling on what a stranger can cost
# you.
#
# Be clear-eyed about what the per-visitor cap is: a signed cookie, and
# nothing more. A caller that simply never sends the cookie is served as a
# fresh visitor every time. That is the accepted "soft cap" from the spec —
# it shapes honest behaviour for real people in browsers, and a scripted
# caller ignores it entirely.
#
# POST /api/free-runs refunds a run only against a signed token that
# /api/analyze issues on a terminal error, so a successful run never yields
# one. The token binds to the charged count, not to a session, so a token can
# be redeemed again once a later charge returns the counter to that same
# value. That is a real weakness and it is documented rather than hidden —
# but it grants nothing beyond the cookie-less path above, which is why it is
# not treated as the thing standing between a stranger and your bill.
#
# The circuit breaker stops one warm instance hammering an exhausted quota;
# it does not bound spend either.
HOSTED_PROVIDER_API_KEY=

# Which provider serves hosted runs: "groq" or "gemini". Optional — falls
# back to the app default provider when unset. If set, it must match a known
# provider id exactly (trimmed); an unrecognized value now refuses hosted
# analysis rather than silently substituting the default, since that
# substitution previously sent the owner's key to the wrong provider.
HOSTED_PROVIDER=groq

# HMAC secret for the free-run counter cookie. Must be at least 16 characters;
# anything shorter disables hosted runs rather than metering them insecurely.
# Generate one:
#   node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
FREE_RUN_SECRET=
